        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Merv</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 550 BCE – 1789 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The first city of Merv was founded in the 6th century BCE as part of the Achaemenid expansion under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a>; archaeological surveys show village life on the site from the 3rd millennium BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-niger-delta">inland delta</a> of the Murghab river on the southern edge of the Karakum Desert, about 30 km east of the city of Mary in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The capital of the Achaemenid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margiana">Margiana</a>; the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution">Abbasid Revolution</a> of 746 to 750; the residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mamun">al-Ma'mun</a> from 813 to 818; the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Great Seljuk Empire</a>; its libraries and scholars; the Mongol capture of 1221; the Tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar">Ahmad Sanjar</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">The site is preserved by the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a> as the State Historical and Cultural Park Ancient Merv, established in 1987, and is listed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
