    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Merv grew from a prehistoric oasis settlement into a satrapal centre under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, and was then ruled in turn by Hellenistic kings, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirids</a>, Ghaznavids and Seljuqs.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-muslim">Abu Muslim</a> declared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid dynasty</a> at Merv in 748, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mamun">al-Ma'mun</a> lived there from 813 to 818, and under the Seljuqs the city reached its greatest size and became the capital of the whole empire from 1118.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> took the city in 1221 with great loss of life, it never regained its former prosperity, and in 1788 and 1789 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-murad">Shah Murad of Bukhara</a> razed it and deported its people.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Merv may have been the largest city in the world in the 12th and 13th centuries, with a population of up to 500,000; Tertius Chandler gave it 200,000 by 1150.</p></aside>
    </section>

